    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0305" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/5342: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-06T17:00:00+01:00">May 6, 1937—5 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 6—4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>256. My despatch No. 1276, April 27,<anchor n="77" xml:id="d190-f1"/> on the
                    fading prestige of Largo Caballero, am informed directly from Del Vayo that his
                    mysterious stay in Paris is concerned with the plan determined upon to replace
                    Caballero without delay. The indications all point to Prieto as the successor
                    since he is backed up [omission] forces. A smaller element would prefer
                    Araquistain, Ambassador in Paris, but his friends and he himself will acquiesce
                    in choice of Prieto. Del Vayo’s conferences with Araquistain are on this
                    subject.</p>
                <pb facs="0306" n="294" xml:id="pg294"/>
                <p>Am sending by today’s pouch photostat reproduction of a memorandum in the alleged
                    handwriting of Goicoechea<anchor n="78" xml:id="d190-f2"/> on agreement reached
                    in Rome March 31, 1934, between representatives of the Monarchist and Carlist
                    parties and Spanish military officers and Mussolini in which the latter pledges
                    assistance in the destruction of existing Spanish regime. This paper taken in
                    raid on Monarchist headquarters in Madrid in August and sent to Foreign Office
                    and not examined until recently. Del Vayo will not embarrass England and France
                    by exercising his right to demand a special meeting of the League of Nations but
                    will place this matter on the agenda for the regular meeting the latter part of
                    the month.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
